&lt;li style=&quot;font-style: italic;&quot; data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Communication from Tide will only come from an official&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;@tide&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;.co&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;email address.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-style: italic;&quot; data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Tide does not work with agencies or recruiters without prior formal engagement, and we do not authorize third parties to make job offers on our behalf.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;If you are contacted by anyone misrepresenting Tide or requesting payment, please treat it as fraudulent and report it to us immediately at &lt;a ----- ----- safety and trust are important to us, and we are committed to ensuring a fair and transparent recruitment process.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;Tide leverages AI to enhance our hiring experience. You can read more about how we use AI in our recruitment process in our &lt;a href=&quot;https://assets.ctfassets.net/3h69mkdgxn20/5MFtWSdG8YLKq3jZkK52NY/3f18633073e6cdbd03bba4b9791c64f4/Using_AI_throughout_the_Hiring_Process.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;AI Policy&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;Your personal data will be processed by Tide for recruitment purposes and in accordance with &lt;/em&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://assets.ctfassets.net/3h69mkdgxn20/30JAUcDJMlaCwUKt4zoW0j/dd541981a67b6838d6e54537704bc8aa/Tide_Recruitment_Privacy_Notice_Job_Post_Version.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://assets.ctfassets.net/3h69mkdgxn20/1MYf6q4ZMWugpeaROVETBN/526e9c160a2de03576413c81657c6466/Recruitment_Privacy_Notice__Final_Draft__Sep_2024_.pdf&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;Tide&#39;s Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Nebius:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nebius is leading a new era in cloud infrastructure for the global AI economy. We are building a full-stack AI cloud platform that supports developers and enterprises from data and model training through to production deployment, without the cost and complexity of building large in-house AI/ML infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Built by engineers, for engineers. From large-scale GPU orchestration to inference optimization, we own the hard problems across compute, storage, networking and applied AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Listed on Nasdaq (NBIS) and headquartered in Amsterdam, we have a global footprint with R&amp;amp;D hubs across Europe, the UK, North America and Israel. Our team of 1,500+ includes hundreds of engineers with deep expertise across hardware, software and AI R&amp;amp;D.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nebius is looking for a Senior / Lead Program Manager to help develop and execute our asset-light model for expanding AI infrastructure through partnerships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work at the intersection of strategy, finance, commercial negotiations and execution. Your focus will be to turn complex partnership opportunities into clear business cases, workable commercial terms and agreements that support the needs of Nebius, our partners and our customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role suits someone who combines structured problem-solving with strong financial understanding and the ability to move work forward across multiple teams. You should be comfortable assessing commercial trade-offs, bringing clarity to ambiguous problems and taking responsibility for progress.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an individual contributor role with significant cross-functional responsibility. You will lead projects and influence stakeholders without direct line-management responsibility.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop commercial frameworks and term sheets.&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Define proposed terms for asset-light partnerships, balancing financial returns, risk, responsibilities and the interests of Nebius and its partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support the partnership team&lt;/strong&gt;.&amp;nbsp;Build the operational framework, track and report progress, develop commercial guidelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build business cases with Finance.&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Coordinate the analysis supporting partnership proposals, working through financial models, testing assumptions and assessing how different commercial terms affect the economics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape contractual and legal structures.&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Partner with Legal and relevant business teams to translate the commercial model into practical structures and agreements for partners and customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive cross-functional execution.&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Bring together Finance, Legal, commercial, technical and operational stakeholders, establishing clear ownership, resolving dependencies and maintaining momentum.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Prepare decisions and recommendations.&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Turn complex information into clear options, explain trade-offs and help stakeholders reach informed decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop repeatable ways of working.&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Capture lessons from individual partnerships and improve the frameworks, templates and processes that support the model as it grows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in management consulting or a strategy and operations role within a technology business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to break down unfamiliar, complex problems and develop practical recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Financial fluency: you can read and work with financial models, challenge assumptions and explain the commercial implications of the numbers. A specialist financial analyst background is not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing business cases, assessing commercial opportunities or supporting complex transactions and partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confidence working with commercial terms and contracts alongside finance and legal specialists.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong stakeholder management skills, including the ability to align teams with different priorities and influence without formal authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The initiative and judgment to drive projects independently, manage ambiguity and recognise when a decision needs wider input.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written and verbal communication, particularly when presenting analysis and recommendations to senior stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Revenue operations background: Supporting sales or partnership teams with clear processes, compensation structure etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience that would be valuable&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work on large, complex projects in data centres, digital infrastructure, real estate, power or related sectors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Revenue operations background: supporting sales or partnership teams with clear processes, compensation structure etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to partnership models, infrastructure economics or arrangements involving several commercial counterparties.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience taking a strategic recommendation through negotiation and into implementation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sector experience is valuable, but we are also interested in strong generalists who can learn a new business model quickly and apply sound commercial judgment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Why join Nebius&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nebius is scaling a new generation of AI infrastructure across EMEA. You will have genuine ownership of how that infrastructure is designed, standardised and delivered, working on complex projects where technical judgement has a direct impact on speed, capacity and long-term operational performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation and benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Career growth and continuous learning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibility, trust and real ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An international environment with highly experienced technical teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The opportunity to shape infrastructure that powers the next generation of AI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nebius is an equal opportunity employer committed to an inclusive workplace. We provide equal employment opportunities and do not discriminate on any characteristic protected by applicable law. Please tell us if you need an accommodation during the application process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits &amp;amp; Perks:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Career growth and learning opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibility and ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative and innovative culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to work on impactful AI projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;International environment and talented teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What&#39;s it like to work at Nebius:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fast moving&amp;nbsp;- Bold thinking&amp;nbsp;- Constant growth&amp;nbsp;- Meaningful impact&amp;nbsp;- Trust and real ownership&amp;nbsp;- Opportunity to shape the future of AI&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nebius is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and diverse workplace and to providing equal employment opportunities in all aspects of employment. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), national origin, ancestry, age, disability, genetic information, marital status, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants must be authorized to work in the country in which they apply and will be required to provide proof of employment eligibility as a condition of hire.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you need accommodations during the application process, please let us know.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Scientist | Semiconductor Metrology&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Abingdon, UK&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reward and Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;£42,000 - £55,000 (depending on experience)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual bonus, 3x salary death in service benefit and private health care BUPA, EMI Share scheme.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are a Data Scientist who enjoys turning instrument data into proof of what is possible, why not join us in Abingdon, Oxfordshire, and help prove the analysis methods behind advanced semiconductor metrology systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an ambitious and adaptable Data Scientist to join our new Data Science team in the Technology department, reporting to the Data Science Lead and working closely with our Modelling Scientist. You will generate and curate data, develop and test new algorithms, and benchmark them against what the instrument can physically deliver. When a method proves itself, you will package it for the Data Analysis team in Engineering, who turn it into robust product software. You will work with real customer use cases and wafer data from Applications Development, and proof-of-concept data from R&amp;amp;D.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are an AI-first team, so you will use AI tools every day, while checking carefully what they produce. If your passion is speed, evidence and finding out what the data can really tell you, we’d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll be doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate synthetic data, and build and maintain the demo and performance data libraries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyse instrument data to quantify noise and limitations, and help establish the information limit, meaning what is physically extractable from the instrument&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and test new algorithms and analysis methods (for example PCA, percentile methods and machine learning) on real and synthetic data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Benchmark methods against the information limit: achievable performance, measurement uncertainty, gauge R&amp;amp;R and drift contributors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write clean, reproducible prototype code with test data and expected performance, ready to hand over to Data Analysis, and build analysis tools used across the Technology department&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI tools every day to code, explore, analyse and report faster, verify what they produce, and present your results to the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education and experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree or above in Physics, Data Science, Applied Mathematics, Engineering or a similar subject, or [2] years’ relevant experience in data science or quantitative research&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills and experience we’re looking for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data analysis in Python (NumPy, SciPy, pandas, scikit-learn or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Heavy, day-to-day use of AI tools in your technical work, such as coding assistants and LLMs, with the judgement to verify their outputs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Image or signal processing, ideally on data from scientific instruments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Statistics applied to measurement data: uncertainty, repeatability, noise and drift&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Machine learning methods, and how to validate them properly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, reproducible code and reports&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explaining results to technical and non-technical colleagues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curious and adaptable, happy to work quickly and test ideas against the evidence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’d love to see:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Atomic Force Microscopy or other nano-characterisation (SEM, FIB, profilometry), or semiconductor metrology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Physics-based modelling or simulation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Version control (Git) and C#, and experience building agentic or AI-assisted analysis workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A bit about us:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Infinitesima is a privately owned company founded in 2001, as a spin-out of the University of Bristol, by CTO Professor Andrew Humphris. Our dynamic team of scientists and engineers is focussed on enabling the next generation of semiconductor devices through delivery of innovative products to customers around the world.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our strength lies in the varied perspectives that come from different cultures, experiences, and identities. We believe that true innovation is fuelled by collaboration, locally and globally. We strive to foster an environment where everyone can contribute meaningfully and thrive.&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;If you require adjustments to take part in the recruitment process, please let us know, we’ll do our best to support you.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:210,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:210,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:300}&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your recruitment journey:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:210,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:210,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:300}&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We will interview you: Monday to Friday UK Time 9am to 4.30pm and we&#39;ll be as flexible as we can with Global Scheduling&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:210,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:210,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:300}&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1st stage:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;(45 minute) Remote meeting to evaluate your experience and technical ability&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2nd stage:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;(2.5 hours) Face to face onsite evaluating technical, presentation and communication skills along with your ways of working and your opportunity to to know more about us&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;If you&#39;re not comfortable with eye contact, let us know at the start of your interview and if REMOTE, once we&#39;ve said hello, feel free to turn your camera off until the end.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We dress casually so informal attire is absolutely fine for onsite interviews. We want you to feel comfortable when you meet us and if there&#39;s anything else we can do to support your journey, just let us know.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A note on how we use AI:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;We use AI&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;only&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;to transcribe our interviews so we can focus fully on you instead of scribbling notes. The AI does&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;not&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;take part in any decision making at any stage. All hiring decisions are made by real humans based on the conversation we have with you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location and working pattern:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;We recognise the value of flexibility and offer a hybrid working model wherever possible. Most employees work onsite three days per week, although some positions require a greater onsite presence due to the nature of the work and business need&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Recruitment agencies: Infinitesima Ltd only works with approved agencies and does not accept unsolicited agency CVs. Please do not submit candidate details in response to this advert or solicit any Infinitesima Ltd employees. Infinitesima Ltd is not responsible for any fees related to unsolicited CVs.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Science Lead | Semiconductor Metrology&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Abingdon, UK&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reward and Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;£70,000 - £85,000 (depending on experience)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual bonus, 3x salary death in service benefit and private health care BUPA, EMI Share scheme.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are a Data Science Lead who enjoys turning measurement data into proof of what is possible, why not join us in Abingdon, Oxfordshire, and build and lead the Data Science team behind advanced semiconductor metrology systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an ambitious and adaptable Data Science Lead to set up a new Data Science team in our Technology department, reporting to the Technology Director. You will lead a small team, initially a Data Scientist and a Modelling Scientist, and stay hands-on as a working lead data scientist. You will explore and prove new analysis methods, from synthetic data and information-limit studies to modelling, machine learning and AI, to improve the performance of our Metron3D systems and draw more insight from our data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work hand in hand with the Data Analysis team in Engineering: you prove what is possible, they make it robust and shippable. You will also collaborate with R&amp;amp;D, System Design Engineering and Applications Development. We are an AI-first team, and you will set the standard for using AI tools well and safely. If your passion is speed, evidence and finding out what the data can really tell you, we’d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll be doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, develop and mentor the Data Science team while staying hands-on, setting priorities and keeping a fast, evidence-based working rhythm&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and deliver the Data Science roadmap: synthetic data, modelling, information-limit studies, algorithm development and data analysis tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish the information limit, meaning what is physically extractable given instrument noise, limitations and tip geometry, and use it as the benchmark for every new method&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explore, test and benchmark new algorithms (for example PCA, percentile methods and machine learning) on real and synthetic data, covering achievable performance, measurement uncertainty and gauge capability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the handover to Data Analysis in Engineering (prototype code, test data, acceptance criteria and expected performance), and manage the demo and performance data libraries with Applications Development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI tools every day, set the team’s standards for using them well and safely, and track the state of the art in third-party and open-source methods&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education and experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MSc or PhD in Physics, Data Science, Applied Mathematics, Engineering or a similar subject, or [8] years’ relevant experience in data science or quantitative research, including some team leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills and experience we’re looking for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading or mentoring a team of data scientists, scientists or engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on data science in Python (NumPy, SciPy, pandas, scikit-learn or similar), turning exploratory work into quantified results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Heavy, day-to-day use of AI tools in your own technical work, such as coding assistants, LLMs and agentic workflows, with a critical eye for checking their outputs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Image processing, signal processing or statistical analysis of measurement data from scientific instruments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Statistical methods for measurement systems: uncertainty, repeatability, gauge R&amp;amp;R and drift&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Machine learning and/or physics-based modelling, with the judgement to pick the right tool for the problem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communication of results to technical and non-technical audiences, with evidence-based recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable setting a roadmap and priorities, and knowing when a result is good enough to hand over&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’d love to see:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Atomic Force Microscopy or other nano-characterisation (SEM, FIB, profilometry), or semiconductor metrology and process control&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Synthetic data generation or forward modelling of instruments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building AI-assisted workflows or tooling for a team (agents, automated analysis pipelines, shared prompt libraries), and handing prototypes to software teams to productionise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A bit about us:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Infinitesima is a privately owned company founded in 2001, as a spin-out of the University of Bristol, by CTO Professor Andrew Humphris. Our dynamic team of scientists and engineers is focussed on enabling the next generation of semiconductor devices through delivery of innovative products to customers around the world.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our strength lies in the varied perspectives that come from different cultures, experiences, and identities. We believe that true innovation is fuelled by collaboration, locally and globally. We strive to foster an environment where everyone can contribute meaningfully and thrive.&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;If you require adjustments to take part in the recruitment process, please let us know, we’ll do our best to support you.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:210,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:210,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:300}&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your recruitment journey:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
